  "notes": "The declared crunk revivalist, and the densest kit in this batch by design — the research calls it \"crunk at maximum density\". That is authored literally: kick 4–6 a bar at `syncopation` 0.5, clap doubled with snare on 3, continuous 16th cowbell (`percs.densityPerBar` 7–11 at 0 dB across four lanes, gang shouts included as a percussion lane), and 16th hats at `fillDensity` 0.5. The tempo is deliberately above the 78 BPM crunk anchor — 156–180 straight — because his records are the faster, more frantic read of that era. The 808 is saturated to distortion (`distortion` heavy, wet 0.35–0.6) on root and fifth, with a mid-bass second layer on the rock material that is not modeled as its own part. Harmony is a one-bar synth ostinato over ♭II/VI stabs, so `melody.phraseBars` carries 1 and the chords are `open` triads low in the register, doubling as the power-chord guitar. ⚠ The live-guitar wing is the genuinely unusual parameter and it is modeled as an **answer part, not a loop**: `countermelody` at 0.5 with `answer_lick` leading, which is the nearest the engine has to a guitarist improvising against the track. ⚠ `medium`, per the research: the crunk-revival intent, the live-guitar practice and the guest architecture are sourced **and the numeric tempo band is inferred**. ⛔ The research says 32nd snare-roll crescendos every 4 bars; the roll here is straight 16ths on an 8/16-bar cadence, which is this batch's fill signature and exists so no two authors write the same fill. The crescendo is carried instead by the widest `velocityRampRange` in the batch (44–98), `rampJitter` 24 and `pitchWalk` 5. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 42 to 37 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 38 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 5. ⚠ **The 1-bar phrase length was removed** (was [1,2], now [2,4]). A one-bar phrase looped four times carries less entropy than a four-bar phrase, and it is the countermelody it strangles hardest: a counter answers *inside* the melody’s phrase, so a one-bar shape leaves it nowhere to go. Every worst offender on `counter.rs` carried it. ⛔ The previous session recorded this exact mistake and it arrived again from the other direction — distinctness is combinatorial in the shape LENGTH, not in the option count.",
